Package: gtk3sermo
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libgtk-3-0 (>= 3.22), libvte-2.91-0
Breaks: haplo-dialog (<< 1.0.0-9)
Replaces: haplo-dialog (<< 1.0.0-9)
Description: GTK 3 dialog boxes for shell scripts (gtkdialog successor)
 gtk3sermo builds native GTK 3 windows from an XML description, so a shell
 script can show a real graphical interface without any toolkit knowledge.
 .
 It is a maintained, hardened fork of gtkdialog (Laszlo Pere, Thunor) and reads
 the same XML: existing gtkdialog scripts run unchanged. 43 widgets. Install the
 gtksermo package if you also want the gtkdialog command name itself.
 .
 Hardening: safe_exec (no system()), FORTIFY_SOURCE=3, PIE, Full RELRO,
 stack-protector-strong.
 .
 Part of the haplo-dialog suite, alongside gtk4sermo (GTK 4). Both install
 side by side.
 .
 Drop-in replacement for gtkdialog: same XML language, same command-line
 interface, same behaviour — verified against a 55-case test corpus. Scripts
 written for gtkdialog need no change.
 .
 Not to be confused with the gtk3dialog package distributed by BunsenLabs,
 which is a different fork of the same ancestor.

Package: gtksermo
Architecture: all
Depends: gtk3sermo (>= ${source:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Conflicts: gtkdialog, gtk3dialog, haplo-dialog
Provides: gtkdialog
Replaces: gtkdialog, haplo-dialog
Description: compatibility command gtkdialog for gtk3sermo
 Installs /usr/bin/gtkdialog as a link to gtk3sermo, so that existing
 scripts written for the original gtkdialog keep working unchanged.
 .
 This package is SEPARATE on purpose. The name gtkdialog is also used
 by other projects: the original gtkdialog, the gtk3dialog package
 shipped by BunsenLabs, and the Puppy Linux builds. Only one package
 may own /usr/bin/gtkdialog, so installing this one conflicts with
 those. Keeping the link out of gtk3sermo lets gtk3sermo and gtk4sermo
 be installed alongside any of them, and makes the trade-off an
 explicit choice rather than a surprise.
 .
 Install it if you want the gtkdialog command. Leave it out to compare
 implementations side by side.
